# Local dependencies and downloaded source trees
node_modules/
.tools/
.wrangler/

# Rust build output from every benchmark adapter and downloaded dependency
**/target/

# Raw benchmark output is retained locally and shared as a separate evidence
# archive. New runs use date/provider suffixes, so ignore every results tree.
results*/
*.jsonl
*.stdout
*.stderr
*.log

# Generated aggregate data and diagnostic output. The selected reviewer-facing
# reports and charts below are intentionally committed instead.
*-analysis*.json
distributed-analysis*.json
media-analysis*.json
moq-analysis.json
moq-data-analysis-gcp.json
moq-stress-analysis.json
cloudflare-startup-observations-gcp.json

# Generated figures are opt-in. This prevents preliminary and diagnostic plots
# from being staged accidentally while retaining the two frozen final figures.
*.png
*.svg
!fair-media-benchmark-all-zones.png
!fair-media-benchmark-all-zones.svg
!transport-benchmark-full-all-zones.png
!transport-benchmark-full-all-zones.svg

# Historical reports describe superseded qualification runs. They remain in
# the local research tree but are not part of the vendor-review packet.
GCP-BENCHMARK-REPORT.md
MEDIA-BENCHMARK.md
REPORT.md
render-cloudflare-managed-moq-preliminary.mjs
render-focused-media-verdict.mjs
render-gcp-comparison.mjs
render-preliminary-moq-comparison.mjs

# Benchmark credentials and short-lived certificates must never be committed.
*.jwk
*.jwt
*.key
*.pem
*.crt
*.csr
*.cnf
*.srl

# Common local noise
.DS_Store
*~
